# tools/kconfig — Linux Kconfig configuration frontends (vendored)

This directory contains the Linux kernel Kconfig configuration frontends,
extracted verbatim from the Linux kernel tree (scripts/kconfig, Linux v6.12)
and used to configure the XJ380 / Code-Cube kernel.

- Upstream: https://github.com/torvalds/linux  (scripts/kconfig, v6.12)
- License:  GNU General Public License, version 2 (GPL-2.0-only)
  See the repository top-level LICENSE file.

## Contents
- Frontends: conf.c, mconf.c, nconf.c, gconf.c, qconf.cc
- Parser:    lexer.l, parser.y (+ generated lexer.lex.c / parser.tab.c at build time)
- Core:      confdata.c, expr.c, symbol.c, menu.c, preprocess.c, util.c
- Dialog:    lxdialog/ (used by mconf)
- Headers:   include/ (list.h, hashtable.h, hash.h, xalloc.h, ...)

## Building the host tools
The Linux kbuild Makefile (kconfig/Makefile) needs the full kbuild macro set
and is not used here. Instead, Makefile.gnos provides a standalone host-tool
build for `conf` and `mconf`:

    make -f tools/kconfig/Makefile.gnos OUT=out/kconfig out/kconfig/conf out/kconfig/mconf

The main Makefile invokes this automatically via the `defconfig` / `menuconfig`
/ `oldconfig` / `config` / `savedefconfig` targets.
